# radroots_runtime_paths

This is the README for `radroots_runtime_paths`, which provides canonical,
typed runtime paths for the `radroots` core libraries.

## Overview

 * validated service and instance identifiers for the sole canonical
   `services/<service>/<instance>` namespace;
 * an injected platform, host-environment, and profile resolver with no ambient
   process-environment constructor;
 * a sealed `RuntimeContext` as the only public service-instance path
   construction boundary;
 * non-forgeable service path and common-artifact views with immutable
   accessors; and
 * pure shared geonames and runtime-store path helpers that do not participate
   in service-instance path selection.

The former generic app/service/worker/shared namespace, raw root containers,
path overrides, process-environment selectors, and bootstrap path helpers are
intentionally removed. Callers must construct typed bootstrap provenance and
resolve a `RuntimeContext` from an explicitly injected resolver.

